WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.659
The drone's first button, u

2
00:00:05.659 --> 00:00:08.122
moves it one metre east

3
00:00:08.122 --> 00:00:10.290
two north and one up.

4
00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:14.527
Its second button, v, moves it one, three

5
00:00:14.527 --> 00:00:15.027
two.

6
00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:16.716
They look alike.

7
00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:17.642
How alike?

8
00:00:17.642 --> 00:00:20.251
Today one number answers that

9
00:00:20.251 --> 00:00:21.681
the dot product

10
00:00:21.765 --> 00:00:25.131
and it also tells us when two directions

11
00:00:25.215 --> 00:00:26.730
are perpendicular.

12
00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.302
Here is a puzzle.

13
00:00:29.302 --> 00:00:34.139
u dot v is nine, and u dot w is ten

14
00:00:34.139 --> 00:00:38.322
for w equal to ten, zero, zero.

15
00:00:38.322 --> 00:00:42.898
Which pair points closer together?

16
00:00:42.898 --> 00:00:45.120
Pause and think.

17
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.775
The dot product multiplies matching

18
00:00:51.863 --> 00:00:55.377
entries and adds them up: one times one

19
00:00:55.377 --> 00:00:59.067
plus two times three, plus one times two

20
00:00:59.067 --> 00:00:59.594
nine.

21
00:00:59.594 --> 00:01:03.460
It is a single number, a transpose times b.

22
00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:07.956
A matrix product is a table of dot products.

23
00:01:07.956 --> 00:01:11.066
Put u and v as the columns of A

24
00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.893
A transpose A holds their dot

25
00:01:13.987 --> 00:01:17.380
products with each other, six, nine

26
00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.170
nine and fourteen.

27
00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.925
The dot product of a vector with

28
00:01:23.024 --> 00:01:25.902
itself is its length squared.

29
00:01:25.902 --> 00:01:30.169
Walk along u: one east, two north, one up.

30
00:01:30.169 --> 00:01:34.237
Pythagoras gives one plus four plus one

31
00:01:34.237 --> 00:01:37.710
six, so u is root six metres long.

32
00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:41.905
In the same way, v has length root fourteen.

33
00:01:41.992 --> 00:01:44.963
Divide u by its length and you get

34
00:01:45.051 --> 00:01:47.934
the unit vector in its direction

35
00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.420
with length one.

36
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.607
The angle comes from the dot product too

37
00:01:53.695 --> 00:01:57.213
a dot b equals the two lengths times the

38
00:01:57.301 --> 00:02:00.204
cosine of the angle between them.

39
00:02:00.204 --> 00:02:03.899
For u and v, the cosine is nine over root

40
00:02:03.987 --> 00:02:06.098
six times root fourteen

41
00:02:06.098 --> 00:02:08.649
about zero point nine eight

42
00:02:08.649 --> 00:02:11.640
an angle of about eleven degrees.

43
00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:14.893
Turn the picture, and you can see how close

44
00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.310
the two buttons are.

45
00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.604
A cosine is never more than one

46
00:02:19.689 --> 00:02:22.658
so a dot product is never more than

47
00:02:22.743 --> 00:02:25.033
the two lengths multiplied

48
00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:28.256
nine is at most nine point one seven.

49
00:02:28.256 --> 00:02:30.970
That is the Schwarz inequality.

50
00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.815
Now the puzzle.

51
00:02:32.815 --> 00:02:37.001
w is ten, zero, zero, and u dot w is ten

52
00:02:37.001 --> 00:02:38.596
more than nine.

53
00:02:38.596 --> 00:02:41.187
But w is ten metres long

54
00:02:41.187 --> 00:02:45.174
the cosine is only zero point four one

55
00:02:45.174 --> 00:02:48.263
an angle of sixty six degrees.

56
00:02:48.263 --> 00:02:52.250
A big dot product is not a small angle

57
00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:55.240
always divide by the lengths.

58
00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:58.030
When the dot product is zero

59
00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:00.698
the cosine is zero: a right angle.

60
00:03:00.698 --> 00:03:03.290
That is what perpendicular means

61
00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:05.500
in any number of dimensions.

62
00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:10.164
Back to the robot matrix M, with rows one

63
00:03:10.164 --> 00:03:12.218
two and three, six.

64
00:03:12.218 --> 00:03:16.634
Its rows lie on the line through one, two.

65
00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:20.639
Its nullspace is the line through two

66
00:03:20.639 --> 00:03:21.769
minus one.

67
00:03:21.769 --> 00:03:23.618
One, two dot two

68
00:03:23.618 --> 00:03:27.110
minus one is two minus two: zero.

69
00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:28.650
Perpendicular.

70
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:32.596
And Pythagoras holds: their sum, three, one

71
00:03:32.596 --> 00:03:34.557
has length squared ten

72
00:03:34.557 --> 00:03:36.600
which is five plus five.

73
00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:39.070
This is no accident.

74
00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:43.228
M x equals zero says row one dot x is zero

75
00:03:43.228 --> 00:03:45.779
and row two dot x is zero.

76
00:03:45.873 --> 00:03:48.519
So every nullspace vector is

77
00:03:48.614 --> 00:03:51.165
perpendicular to every row

78
00:03:51.165 --> 00:03:54.756
and to every combination of the rows

79
00:03:54.756 --> 00:03:56.740
the whole row space.

80
00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.724
Part two shows the same for the drone

81
00:03:59.793 --> 00:04:02.357
where the row space and the nullspace

82
00:04:02.427 --> 00:04:04.090
live in four dimensions.

83
00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:05.035
So

84
00:04:05.035 --> 00:04:10.150
a dot b adds the products of the entries.

85
00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:13.924
a dot a is the length squared.

86
00:04:14.046 --> 00:04:17.942
The cosine of the angle is a dot

87
00:04:18.064 --> 00:04:21.230
b divided by both lengths.

88
00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:25.237
A zero dot product means perpendicular

89
00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:29.270
and the rows of a matrix are perpendicular

90
00:04:29.363 --> 00:04:30.958
to its nullspace.

91
00:04:30.958 --> 00:04:34.240
Your turn: find the length of two

92
00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.740
minus one, two.
